// WAF rule profiling, for tuning a ruleset from evidence rather than from guesswork.
//
// A WAF console shows what a rule DID. Deciding what it SHOULD do needs three things it
// does not show: whether the requests it matched actually looked like attacks, which
// sites and URLs they arrived on, and whether any other vendor independently agreed.
// This surface answers those, and stops there — it reports evidence and never generates
// configuration, because the decision to enforce or exempt a rule belongs to the person
